Band Visual & Press Photoshoot Prompt: A grim, brutalist concrete dockyard at dusk, heavy industrial fog rolling in from the unseen sea. The Rust-Bellow stands amidst abandoned shipping containers and rusted cranes, backlit by flickering floodlights. Kalpana, in a modified orange boiler suit with reflective hazard stripes crudely painted on, holds a vintage, rust-pocked microphone, her face a mask of primal scream and focused intensity. Silas, wearing a patched denim vest over a thick thermal shirt, straddles his mangled guitar, which seems to sprout metallic tendrils, smoke coiling from its pickups. Jaga, bare-chested under a dark work apron, is poised over his intricate, scrap-metal drum kit, mallets raised, muscles tense, his eyes burning with a cold fire. The air is thick with visible sound waves and the smell of industrial decay, creating an aesthetic of raw, post-apocalyptic utility and contained violence.

Descriptive Mood or Vibe: Post-industrial catharsis, maritime existentialism, mechanical dread, sonic dereliction.

